      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If I remember correctly, anything below 0.001 would cause many issues, including issues using the UI on desktop (the mouse would move in a grid-like pattern etc) and would be completely unusable.\nI think that 0.001-0.005 would be a safe limit to experiment with, however there definitely is potential that it would cause issues with certain worlds/setups that make no sense.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "62eab73e4cf0fc0e1baeb614",
      "author": {
        "_id": "60ac2099dee27167fa4ff7f5",
        "alias": "Green Hamster",
        "aliasID": "65c384dfed6eefce4cdbf582",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/3b3cf8ed5adb45a991520ee8968d7662.png",
        "created": "2021-05-24T21:54:33.380Z",
        "name": "Megacrafter127",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-08-03T17:58:22.433Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62e4dfe321575b44a23e6010",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "One way to avoid some issues of a too small near clip plane would be to also move the far clip plane as well, thus keeping the required depth buffer precision identical. Downside is that the far clip plane has to be moved much more than the near clip plane (e.g. if you halve the distance to the near clip plane, you also have to halve the distance to the far clip plane to keep the required depth buffer resolution identical)\nHowever, small worlds do not need faraway far clip planes, so it might be worth it to expose a setting for whether or not near clip adjustment also adjusts far clip plane to avoid visual artifacts.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-30T07:38:11.051Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "First of all i want to say that i am really happy to see this feature being worked on in the first place.\nThat being said i feel like the way the latest blog post described it is a little bit too limiting.\nIn the blog post the smallest you could set it is 0.01. Before EAC there was a mod with the same name that could set the clipping plane a lot smaller.\nIve seen some really tiny avatars hanging out with the vrchat size community, avatars made possible by mods like scale goes brrr (which is also something id love to see implemented) and needing near clip plane adjust to make them able to see themself.\nEven though at such tiny scales the menu would be quite glitchy, we all still loved using those super tiny avatars. Its such an amazing experience exploring worlds at those extreme scales.\nAnd with the current settings as described in the blog post this is not possible.\nEven though its already a super niche feature, i think it would be amazing to have atleast one slightly smaller clipping plane, maybe something like 0.005. I know the vrchat size community would absolutely love that despite the menus going a little glitchy at that size.",
